// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 490.5pt), 50.5pt, 55pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 59.52pt, "tem provides a convenient model because it is experimentally man-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 74.16pt, "ageable, optically contrasted, and sufficiently simple to allow a clear ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 88.7pt, "interpretation of the classification results. Using laser speckle images ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 103.22pt, "recorded from droplets held in a linear electrodynamic quadrupole ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 117.74pt, "trap [17], we test whether a CNN can recognize selected droplet and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 132.26pt, "suspension parameters. Specifically, we consider the determination of ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.9pt, "droplet size, nanoparticle concentration and nanoparticle diameter, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 161.42pt, "first separately and then in simultaneous two-parameter and three-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 175.94pt, "parameter classification tasks. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 200.54pt, "The present study is therefore intended as a proof of principle for ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 215.06pt, "data-driven multi-parameter recognition in levitated suspension mi-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 229.58pt, "crodroplets. More broadly, it represents a step toward optical diagnos-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 244.1pt, "tics of more complex aerosol-like systems, including real-world wa-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 258.77pt, "ter-based droplets and suspensions, for which conventional feature ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 273.29pt, "engineering may prove insufficient. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 297.77pt, "We report that we successfully progressed from single-parameter to ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 312.41pt, "multiple-parameter classification of microdroplets of suspension. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 326.93pt, "Here, for speed, we restricted ourselves to 27 classes, while from our ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 341.45pt, "previous works we know that the number of classes is mostly limited ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 355.97pt, "only by computational resources. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 380.57pt, "In this work, we also limited ourselves to monodisperse (colloidal) ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 395.09pt, "suspensions of nanoparticles (NPs) in a slowly evaporating liquid, which were easier to handle experimentally ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 409.63pt, "and were expected to yield easier to interpret results. Application of the method to real-world water-based aero-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 424.15pt, "sols remains an ultimate goal. ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#365f91"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 465.91pt, "Experimental setup and procedures ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 481.63pt, "The microdroplets investigated in these experiments were maintained in a custom-built Linear Electrodynamic ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 496.15pt, "Quadrupole Trap (LEQT). The core trap has been described previously in our papers (see e.g. [17,18]), and a ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 510.67pt, "schematic view of the version used here is shown in Figure 1. An electrodynamic trap – also known as an elec-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 525.31pt, "trodynamic balance (EDB) – enables non-contact optical studies of single levitating micro-objects. In this study, ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 539.83pt, "we recorded laser speckles generated by microdroplets of monodisperse nanoparticle suspensions. The initial ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 554.35pt, "concentration of suspension was set in each ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 568.87pt, "experiment, while microdroplets evaporated ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 583.42pt, "slowly, so the microdroplet diameter change ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 598.06pt, "during the experimental run could be considered ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 612.58pt, "negligible and comparable to the accuracy of ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 627.1pt, "diameter measurement (~0.1%) and similarly, ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 641.62pt, "the average suspension concentration could be ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 656.26pt, "considered constant (less than 0.35% change). ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 670.78pt, "The microdroplet diameter was measured with ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 685.3pt, "shadowgraphy (see inset in Figure 4). The total ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 700.66pt, "accuracy of the method was estimated as  ")
  #line-at(529.42pt, 700.66pt, "100 ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 715.3pt, "nm. The contributing uncertainties come from ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 729.94pt, "the optical system resolution and the masquer-")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 744.48pt, "ading effect of microdroplet motion in the trap. ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 759pt, "The estimation of accuracy of initial suspension ")
  #line-at(332.47pt, 773.52pt, "concentration is somewhat difficult due to un-")
