#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-05.png", width: 232pt), 311.5pt, 248pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 59.52pt, "kernel with standard deviation of 2. Then each image was normalized (0–1) between its min and max. This ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 74.16pt, "normalization – also applied in our previous works – ensured that CNNs were trained on image features other ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 88.7pt, "than brightness, which can easily be influenced by unwanted or random factors (droplet size, its momentary ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 103.22pt, "position in the illumination beam, fluctuations of beam power, etc.). Altogether, we collected ~1.5×10")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(506.14pt, 98.18pt, "6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(509.62pt, 103.22pt, " speckle ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 117.74pt, "images. Of these, we were able to construct the needed datasets for the selected parameter set (one, two, and ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 132.26pt, "three parameters), both for training and independent testing (sample images from both datasets can be found at ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.9pt, "[23]). Each frame series was verified by the experimenter against the presence of artifacts. Those spotted or ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 161.42pt, "suspected were excluded from training (see next section). ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 185.9pt, "We used a CNN constructed in [14] and further developed in [16], with further tweaks introduced for the pur-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 200.54pt, "pose of this work. Its schematic representation is shown in Figure 2 and its code can be found at [23]. It is es-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 215.06pt, "sentially a residual multi-branch texture classifier for speckle images: it first extracts local texture patterns, then ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 229.58pt, "refines them through skip-connected blocks, then analyzes them in two parallel feature streams, fuses both ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 244.1pt, "streams, and finally classifies the whole image based on ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 258.77pt, "the resulting global texture signature. Several modifica-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 273.29pt, "tions were tried at the stage of final experiments with 3-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 287.81pt, "parameter classifications. In particular, we tried intro-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 302.33pt, "ducing further differences between the branches of the ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 316.85pt, "network, but  the task seems already near the useful ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 331.49pt, "limit of this architecture. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 355.97pt, "The CNN operated in Matlab (2023a) environment on a ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 370.49pt, "PC with two NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 GPUs. We ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 385.13pt, "used stochastic gradient descent with momentum ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 399.65pt, "(SGDM) algorithm for training. For the (essential) hy-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 414.19pt, "perparameters shown in Table 1, training took from ~60 ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 428.71pt, "minutes for single-parameter tasks to ~600 minutes for ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 443.23pt, "3-parameter task. This, however, can be further fine-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 457.87pt, "tuned. For the single-parameter classification experi-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 472.39pt, "ments, when a more relaxed hyperparameter set can be ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 486.91pt, "used, the training time can be reduced about four-fold. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 511.51pt, "The networks always trained  with validation accuracy ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 526.03pt, "better than 90%, which in case of the classification ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 540.55pt, "tasks we set up may be misleading. Thus, we always ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 555.07pt, "used independent data sets to check whether the net-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 569.71pt, "work generalizes properly. The independent data sets ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 584.26pt, "were constructed of image series from experiment se-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 598.78pt, "quences (days) which were not used for the construction ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 613.3pt, "of the training set, as well as of those from which some ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 627.82pt, "different series were incorporated into the training sets. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 642.46pt, "For each experimental day, the setup was fully restart-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 656.98pt, "ed. Since we did not find any differences in classifica-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 671.5pt, "tion accuracy between those, we are sure that the CNN ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 686.02pt, "did not train on series-specific features. We also cross-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 700.66pt, "verified the training with gradient-weighted class acti-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 715.18pt, "vation mapping (Grad-CAM) technique, to be sure that ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 729.7pt, "the network does not activate in response to image or ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 744.24pt, "experimental artifacts (to avoid the so called “Russian ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 758.76pt, "tank fallacy”). ")
