#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-06.png", width: 222pt), 320pt, 361pt))[
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#365f91"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 62.76pt, "Results ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#4f81bd"))
  #line-at(56.64pt, 90.86pt, "Single-parameter determination of dense suspension microdroplets  ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#4f81bd"))
  #line-at(63.72pt, 116.42pt, "Recognizing diameter of a microdroplet of dense suspension ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 130.82pt, "Differently than in [16], here we trained CNNs on experimentally obtained speckle images from microdroplets. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 145.34pt, "It turned out that assessing the diameter of a microdroplet for a given suspension concentration and NP diameter ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 159.86pt, "using a trained CNN network is quite easy. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 184.46pt, "In Figure 4 we show a series of diameters – obtained from shadowgraphy – of microdroplets with 20 mg/mL ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 198.98pt, "concentration of 100-nm diameter TiO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.61pt, 200.54pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(227.09pt, 198.98pt, " NPs. Since we did not have a precise control over the injected micro-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 213.5pt, "droplet diameter, the diameters were not very evenly spaced: some diameters ranges were overrepresented. To ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 228.14pt, "insure fairly even diameters distribution for CNN training, we excluded “surplus” speckle images – correspond-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 242.66pt, "ing to gray circles in Figure 4 – from training and used them to construct an independent data set instead. If an ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 257.21pt, "artifact was spotted by the experimenter in the collected images (glare, stationary speckle, etc.), the image series ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 271.73pt, "was excluded form training and general testing. However, we also separately tested a trained CNN on a set of ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 286.25pt, "image series assessed by experimenter as infested or suspected of artifacts. Surprisingly, the classification was ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 300.89pt, "quite sensible, though obviously poorer, which indicates that our CNNs actually generalizes very well and the ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 315.41pt, "method is to some extent immune to glitches in the tested images/image series. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 340.73pt, "An example shadowgraphy image is presented in the inset in Figure 4.")
  #line-at(376.63pt, 340.73pt, "It corresponds to a 80.5-")
  #set text(font: "Symbol", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(488.62pt, 340.73pt, "m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(494.98pt, 340.73pt, "m-diameter ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 355.49pt, "microdroplet indicated in the series with the red arrow. A central bright spot – the focal point at the surface of ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 370.01pt, "the sphere (droplet) is plainly visible, which indi-")
