  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.56pt, 59.52pt, "Among the tested quantities, droplet diameter was the most readily recognized parameter, which is consistent ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 74.16pt, "with its relatively strong manifestation in the spatial structure of the speckle patterns. Nanoparticle concentra-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 88.7pt, "tion proved to be a more demanding variable, likely because its influence is encoded in subtler image features ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 103.22pt, "and because the experimental uncertainty of the initial concentration was comparatively large. Even so, classifi-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 117.74pt, "cation remained feasible when concentration classes were sufficiently distinct. Recognition of nanoparticle di-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 132.26pt, "ameter was also successful under the conditions examined, although the present design does not fully separate ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 146.9pt, "particle-size effects from accompanying changes in particle number at fixed mass concentration.")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 171.38pt, "A notable result is that the approach remained effective when extended from single-parameter to simultaneous ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 185.9pt, "two-parameter and three-parameter classification. Although the confusion matrices reveal some residual cross-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 200.54pt, "class similarities, suggesting that certain parameters are represented more strongly than others in the learned ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 215.06pt, "feature space, the overall performance supports the feasibility of multi-parameter recognition in this type of ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 229.58pt, "system. ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 254.21pt, "Overall, the present results should be regarded as a proof-of-principle for a suspension-droplet system. They ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 268.73pt, "suggest that further improvements in concentration control, dataset design, and network architecture could en-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 283.25pt, "hance robustness and resolution. More broadly, the method appears promising as a basis for future optical diag-")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 297.77pt, "nostics of more complex free droplets of suspensions, including more complex aerosol-like systems that may be ")
  #line-at(49.56pt, 312.41pt, "less amenable to conventional feature-based approaches.")
